  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>5b4555fa-c8a5-4719-8c49-fbecfac0f65b</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Tomato cubes, processing, at plant, Northern Italy, 1 kg of tomato cubes</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>1 kg di Cubetti di pomodoro, trasformazione allo stabilimento, Nord Italia </common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Materials production</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Food and renewable raw materials</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The dataset has been developed within the Arcadia Project. It concerns the processing of industrial tomatoes in reference to the report “Studio LCA della filiera dell’industria del pomodoro confezionato in Italia”.</common:generalComment>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2021</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2028</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT">
        <descriptionOfRestrictions>Italy. Primary data collected in the North. Representative dataset of North Italian tomato chain production.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
      </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>For processing tomatoes into tomatoes cubes, the same qualities as for peeled tomatoes are required, with a specific preference toward fruits possessing reduced seed content and greater texture. Mainly round peeled tomatoes are used, cut or pressed through rather large holes. Depending on the type of cutting and pressing, a product which is marketed respectively as pulp, chopped, diced, sliced, is obtained.&#13;
Primary (North Italian supply chain) and secondary (literature and/or industry data) data representative of the North Italian supply chain in terms of geographic characteristics and technologies used (machinery, equipment, etc.) were collected. Inventory data were collected as physical quantities of materials used in different processes. The benefits from the use of secondary materials produced by recycling waste materials (e.g., plastics and cardboard) were excluded.&#13;
Background data were modelled according to Ecoinvent v. 3.8</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Tomatoes cubes are whole and suitable for all those dishes in which the fruit does not disintegrate too much. They can also be crushed to stuff pizza or be used in preparations that call for a thick, full-bodied sauce.</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
